WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:03.169
Previously on "Family Guy":

00:03.293 --> 00:06.005
Oh, my God. Tell your father
not to start the car.

00:08.590 --> 00:12.468
You want my badge number?
Here's my freakin' badge number!

00:13.177 --> 00:16.431
- I can't lose this case.
- Lois, the case is already over.

00:18.099 --> 00:20.059
Who did this to you?!

00:20.185 --> 00:23.813
In all my research,
I've never seen a virus reproduce so fast.

00:30.068 --> 00:32.279
Everyone I told about the file is dead.

00:32.363 --> 00:35.824
What do you mean, "Cut the blue wire"?
They're all blue.

00:37.700 --> 00:41.037
Face it. He's never coming out of that coma.

00:46.334 --> 00:49.045
Aaaargh!

00:49.170 --> 00:52.923
Brian's gone to Los Angeles
to find himself.

00:53.632 --> 00:56.759
"It seems today that all you see

00:56.884 --> 01:00.221
"Is violence in movies and sex on TV

01:00.305 --> 01:03.975
"But where are those
good old-fashioned values

01:04.058 --> 01:06.893
"On which we used to rely?

01:06.978 --> 01:10.105
"Lucky there's a family guy

01:10.229 --> 01:15.110
"Lucky there's a man who positively can do
all the things that make us

01:15.235 --> 01:16.904
"Laugh and cry

01:16.987 --> 01:22.117
"He's a family guy

01:25.537 --> 01:27.622
Don't throw out Brian's things.

01:27.747 --> 01:31.584
He won't be in LA for ever.
He just needs to find himself.

01:31.709 --> 01:35.129
He's not coming back, Lois.
He just walked out on us.

01:35.254 --> 01:37.756
Oh, boy, did we have some good times.

01:38.590 --> 01:40.675
Here it comes, buddy.

01:42.761 --> 01:45.347
Argh! Oh, God! Oh, God!

01:45.472 --> 01:47.015
Argh! Ow!

01:47.140 --> 01:49.225
What are the odds? Argh!

01:49.309 --> 01:52.645
If he does come back,
I want everything to be how he left it.

01:52.770 --> 01:54.938
Easy! Massage the scalp.

01:55.063 --> 01:59.443
You're washing a baby's hair, not
scrubbing vomit off your Christmas dress.

01:59.526 --> 02:02.780
- We got a letter from Brian.
- Tell him I'm not here.

02:02.863 --> 02:05.573
- Let me see.
- Argh! Argh!

02:05.699 --> 02:09.660
Oh, I'm sorry, sweetie.
There. All better?

02:09.744 --> 02:14.040
You are some piece of work, lady.
If you... Actually, yes, it is.

02:15.082 --> 02:18.502
"Greetings from California.
I've been very busy. "

02:18.627 --> 02:21.837
"Having a great time trying
to make it as a writer in LA."

02:21.964 --> 02:24.550
"It's as easy as everyone thinks it is. "

02:24.675 --> 02:29.138
"I've been working the room
at a lot of Hollywood parties. " Oh!

02:31.764 --> 02:34.476
Bobby! Loved you in Raging Bull.

02:34.559 --> 02:36.644
Hey, Jodie, how's the baby?

02:36.769 --> 02:38.855
All right.

02:39.688 --> 02:45.110
I need more cheese puffs. Oprah's off the
wagon. No toothpicks. She'll hurt herself.

02:45.193 --> 02:48.530
Did you hear about Jason?
Paramount bought his script.

02:48.655 --> 02:52.908
- They bought Death Spares Not the Tiger?
- 100 grand. Pretty good, huh?

02:53.033 --> 02:56.371
Sheesh. He's been in LA
how long? Unbelievable.

02:56.454 --> 03:01.042
You know he actually called the main
character John Everyman? Come on.

03:01.168 --> 03:03.336
Well, good for him.

03:13.888 --> 03:16.180
Keanu Reeves. Wow.

03:16.263 --> 03:22.437
I don't usually gush, so forgive me, but when
I was writing Coastguard... Oh, I'm a writer.

03:22.520 --> 03:27.024
When I was writing Coastguard,
I couldn't think of anyone other than...

03:27.107 --> 03:30.987
- There's a woodpecker on your head.
- Yeah, he comes and goes.

03:32.862 --> 03:35.240
Now back to "Kids Say the Darndest Things".

03:35.364 --> 03:38.577
It's OK. Take your time. Then what happened?

03:38.701 --> 03:42.871
He... said he would kill me
if I ever said anything.

03:42.955 --> 03:48.502
- Do you remember what he looked like?
- Yeah. He had a scar on his arm

03:48.586 --> 03:51.087
and he had a big, stupid, doo-doo head.

03:51.212 --> 03:53.799
A big, stupid, doo-doo head!

03:57.051 --> 04:00.596
Oh, honestly, the things
these children come up with.

04:00.680 --> 04:06.102
If you have a child you'd like to exploit to get
a trip to LA, have them try out for our show.

04:06.227 --> 04:09.437
Next auditions in New York
and Quahog, Rhode Island.

04:09.563 --> 04:13.942
- Maybe Stewie could get on that show.
- You must be shrooming.

04:14.025 --> 04:17.071
Yeah! We can get a free trip
to LA and see Brian.

04:17.154 --> 04:21.866
Jeez, I haven't been to California
since I lived with my other family.

04:21.950 --> 04:25.412
Guys, I just got invited to a party
at Sharon Tate's house!

04:25.496 --> 04:29.373
You guys can come, but you gotta
promise not to embarrass me.

04:30.832 --> 04:35.005
Talk! I know you've been plotting
to foil my plans of world domination.

04:35.088 --> 04:38.549
Who are you working for?
The Libyans? The French?

04:38.633 --> 04:43.136
Very well. If torture won't work,
perhaps a little tenderness will.

04:43.219 --> 04:50.434
Mm, I like your taste in women. Yes, she and I
are going to have a good time together.

04:50.517 --> 04:53.145
Yes, you like this, don't you?

04:53.228 --> 04:57.316
Oh, God. Look at me having sex
with a pig. I've become my father.

04:57.399 --> 04:59.818
Stewie, let's get your sailor suit.

04:59.901 --> 05:02.738
You gotta look cute
to audition for national TV.

05:02.821 --> 05:05.658
Lois, I told you. There's no way...

05:05.741 --> 05:09.077
National TV, you say? Coast to coast?

05:09.202 --> 05:15.666
That could be the ideal place to unleash my
hypnosis device on the unsuspecting public.

05:15.749 --> 05:20.753
I always loved this little sailor suit.
Or we could do nice corduroys and a sweater.

05:20.879 --> 05:25.258
Or you could make yourself useful
and wipe my button - circular motion.

05:25.341 --> 05:27.219
And don't you look at me!

05:32.849 --> 05:37.019
Oh, my God. That's Michael Eisner.
I'll take it from here, Julio.

05:39.730 --> 05:42.983
Here you go, Mr Eisner. It's been Brian-ised.

05:43.067 --> 05:45.486
You might notice that new-script smell.

05:45.569 --> 05:48.906
Every car I hand-wash
comes with a smile, an air freshener,

05:49.031 --> 05:53.201
and a copy of my coming-of-age
teen comedy set in Wisconsin.

05:53.284 --> 05:54.953
- What's your name?
- Brian.

05:55.078 --> 05:58.080
Let's see. There we go.

05:58.205 --> 05:59.874
Brian.

05:59.957 --> 06:03.002
See you at Disneyland. Bring money.

06:09.675 --> 06:14.679
Look. It's Tom Tucker from the news.
And that must be his son.

06:14.762 --> 06:18.515
- Oh, my.
- I feel bad staring without having got a ticket.

06:18.640 --> 06:21.769
How can I follow that act?
Bite the head off a chicken?

06:21.853 --> 06:26.148
- Dad, they're staring at me.
- They're just jealous.

06:27.607 --> 06:29.776
- You're next.
- Wait. We were next.

06:29.902 --> 06:33.238
Hey! Hey! Don't walk away from me! Hey!

06:33.864 --> 06:38.952
You know what we'll do? We'll get
the video camera and make our own show.

06:39.077 --> 06:43.456
- I don't wanna.
- Yes, you do. You do because it's normal.

06:44.998 --> 06:48.044
Tell us, Stewie. What job does a mommy do?

06:48.044 --> 06:51.880
Interesting question.
More to the point, how does one define "job"

06:52.005 --> 06:55.217
without branding oneself with useless
labels?

06:55.342 --> 06:59.720
I'm sorry. I'm afraid I answered
your question with another question.

06:59.804 --> 07:02.640
Um... How old do you think Daddy is?

07:02.640 --> 07:04.309
42.

07:04.392 --> 07:09.939
Oh. I mean, Daddy's old. I think he's seven.

07:12.649 --> 07:16.694
That's it. That's what you want to hear.
Yes, jump through the hoop.

07:16.819 --> 07:18.988
Daddy's feet smell.

07:19.113 --> 07:20.991
Jackasses.

07:20.991 --> 07:25.035
Mr and Mrs Griffin, he's adorable.

07:25.160 --> 07:28.289
Congratulations.
Stewie's gonna be on the show.

07:28.372 --> 07:32.960
Did you hear that? We're going to Hollywood,
where people are sexy and clever

07:33.086 --> 07:37.047
and always say somethin' funny
before the commercial break.

07:46.431 --> 07:49.558
Great. I always end up
sitting next to a damn baby.

07:49.642 --> 07:51.310
What did you just say?

07:51.435 --> 07:54.021
- Stewie, stop fussing.
- Not now, Lois.

07:54.146 --> 07:58.109
Turn around. If you've got
something to say, say it to my face.

07:58.192 --> 08:00.694
Oh, you can't hear me now? That's it.

08:00.819 --> 08:04.573
I was going to watch the movie,
but forget it. You're now my bitch.

08:04.656 --> 08:06.866
Wah! Wah!

08:06.950 --> 08:09.993
My ears are popping
and there's no way to console me.

08:10.077 --> 08:15.291
I'm hungry and possibly teething.
Maybe I'm wet. Who knows? I'm a baby.

08:15.415 --> 08:17.710
Wah! Wah!

08:21.881 --> 08:26.760
This is a message
for Brian. This is Jack Nicholson.

08:26.885 --> 08:32.306
Listen, I read your script
and it just jumped right off the page.

08:32.389 --> 08:37.936
I think it's something I'd be excited
to be a part of, so call my...

08:40.022 --> 08:45.444
Listen, I'm just jackin'you. Me and my buddy
Phil just found your script at Starbucks.

08:45.527 --> 08:48.030
- Tell him it sucks.
- Yeah, it sucks.

08:48.155 --> 08:52.325
Give it up, loser, and don't put
your number on the cover, you stupid...

08:52.409 --> 08:55.537
I'm hungry.

08:55.662 --> 08:58.372
Jasper's residence.

08:58.455 --> 09:03.167
- Who the hell is Jasper? Where's Brian?
- Peter? It's me. Jasper's my cousin.

09:03.251 --> 09:06.588
I'm using his place. He's working
at Club Med. Are you on a cell?

09:06.713 --> 09:11.717
- Yeah, we're in LA.
- What? W-What a terrific surprise.

09:11.801 --> 09:17.139
- Brian, can we see you for dinner?
- Yeah, you're not too famous to see us?

09:17.223 --> 09:21.602
Well, I was invited to the premiere
of the new, uh...

09:24.438 --> 09:28.192
the new Val Kilmer picture,
but I'd rather take you out to dinner.

09:28.275 --> 09:33.614
- How about Musso & Frank's at eight?
- OK. See ya later, Mr Big Shot...

09:33.697 --> 09:37.158
Crap. I didn't push "End".
This is gonna cost me a fortune.

09:41.204 --> 09:44.874
Brian! I'm back. Tell me everything.
I'm sitting, I'm hearing.

09:44.957 --> 09:49.044
That's Ricardo. Ricardo, Brian.
He doesn't speak English. Can I? Mm-mm.

09:49.127 --> 09:52.672
Catching up. OK, me first. I'm in love.
Ooh, too much dressing.

09:52.797 --> 09:55.801
He's from the Philippines.
I know - I'm a rice queen.

09:55.926 --> 10:00.305
- How's the writing thingy going?
- Terrible. I can't get my foot in the door.

10:00.388 --> 10:03.850
I have somebody you have to meet.
He's a producer. He's great.

10:03.933 --> 10:06.352
Really? Thanks. That'd be great.

10:06.436 --> 10:09.272
- D'you like sex and the city?
- It's an OK show.

10:09.355 --> 10:12.400
I wasn't talking about the show.
Ooh! I'm nasty.

10:12.483 --> 10:15.610
Someone send me out to sea.

10:17.904 --> 10:22.075
It says here this is the gutter
where the policeman fell over laughing

10:22.201 --> 10:26.037
after Eddie Murphy said he was just
giving the transvestite a ride home.

10:26.162 --> 10:29.164
Oh, I think that's me.

10:29.290 --> 10:31.668
- Hello.
- Hey, Peter. It's Quagmire.

10:31.792 --> 10:35.629
- Hey, Quagmire.
- Last night I had sex with a black chick.

10:35.755 --> 10:38.673
Uh... uh... I gotta go.

10:38.756 --> 10:41.258
- Sorry.
- What? All he said was "black chick".

10:41.384 --> 10:45.763
I know, but your boyfriend looks like
one of your typical angry black guys.

10:45.846 --> 10:50.559
Hey, we cool, G?
Yuh? Yuh? Yuh? All right.

10:53.354 --> 10:58.566
Halle Berry would be perfect as the camp
counsellor all the kids wanna "get with".

10:58.691 --> 11:01.194
Jasper was right. You're very talented.

11:01.277 --> 11:04.822
I'm having a brainstorm.
Ever thought about directing?

11:04.947 --> 11:08.284
- Just every waking hour!
- Well, I got this movie.

11:08.367 --> 11:11.704
It's a low-budget movie,
but the script is solid.

11:11.830 --> 11:16.834
My director quit and I need somebody who's
smart, ambitious and not addicted to meth.

11:16.917 --> 11:19.420
Well, I am smart and ambitious!

11:20.671 --> 11:22.255
- Seriously.
- I'm clean.

11:25.674 --> 11:28.928
Musso & Frank's is famous.
See the bar over there?

11:29.012 --> 11:34.349
- Great writers like Hemingway drank there.
- Where'd that guy who wrote Porky's drink?

11:34.433 --> 11:38.812
Oh, man, when that fat broad grabbed
that kid's crank through the hole.

11:38.937 --> 11:43.108
Where do they get their ideas?
You're the writer. You tell me.

11:43.191 --> 11:48.320
Oh, boy. This is great. All that searching,
that emptiness I felt back home, gone.

11:48.404 --> 11:52.784
- I've finally found my life's calling.
- How wonderful.

11:52.909 --> 11:56.745
I've always found your writing
a little hackneyed and stilted,

11:56.870 --> 12:00.916
but I guess that's why I'm not
workin' out here in Hollywood, huh?

12:01.041 --> 12:06.755
- Oh, congratulations on all your success.
- Uh, thank you.

12:06.880 --> 12:10.633
- Know what might be a thrill for you guys?
- Ooh! Eating a pebble!

12:10.716 --> 12:14.804
Yes, but I was talking about
stopping by the set to see me in action.

12:14.888 --> 12:19.808
- Brian, could we really?
- You do know somebody in the business.

12:19.892 --> 12:23.978
I'm in the business too, you know.
I'm going to be on television.

12:24.062 --> 12:26.899
- Great.
- And when I make my appearance,

12:26.982 --> 12:31.069
- you'll all be talking about it the next day.
- Good luck with that.

12:31.153 --> 12:33.864
"Good luck with that. " Yutz.

12:35.865 --> 12:38.868
- Hello. Peter Griffin?
- You're in him.

12:38.993 --> 12:41.579
Are you happy with
your long-distance service?

12:41.704 --> 12:44.916
Yes, and I'm tired of you people
always calling during dinner.

12:45.041 --> 12:47.751
- Give me your supervisor.
- Hold, please.

12:50.879 --> 12:54.716
Oh, Peter, I love this song.
Open your mouth.

12:59.637 --> 13:02.849
Brian. Right on time. I like that. Come in.

13:02.974 --> 13:05.477
So, ready to shoot your first scene?

13:05.560 --> 13:08.478
- Sure. Where's the set?
- Second door on your left.

13:14.317 --> 13:19.864
- So, this is a shampoo commercial, right?
- Do I have to sleep with the dog in this one?

13:19.948 --> 13:23.409
Can someone fluff Paul?
He's got a windsock thing goin' on.

13:23.493 --> 13:27.038
So, this is a shampoo commercial, right?

13:31.333 --> 13:34.337
Zack, I'm sorry.
There's just no way I can do this.

13:34.462 --> 13:38.007
I've been around.
I've licked my share of peanut butter.

13:38.090 --> 13:41.217
But I think you need
to find yourself a new director.

13:41.342 --> 13:43.635
- Are you sure?
- I just can't do this.

13:43.719 --> 13:47.807
Is this any more degrading than
washing cars? Here you can be creative.

13:47.807 --> 13:54.688
I wanna make this perfectly clear. There is
absolutely no way I would consider doing it.

13:56.024 --> 13:59.568
- Unless I saw a script first.
- Of course.

14:01.986 --> 14:04.990
- This isn't bad.
- It's like Bang the Drum Slowly,

14:05.115 --> 14:06.656
except the drum's a chick.

14:12.621 --> 14:16.250
Peter, slow down. Brian said
he was gonna be on the set all day.

14:16.375 --> 14:22.005
"On the set"! Listen to me. Two days in
Hollywood and I sound like a contract player.

14:24.173 --> 14:26.593
Oh, crap. The LAPD.

14:26.676 --> 14:29.178
Argh! Ow! Argh! Ow!

14:30.346 --> 14:34.099
Come on, Peter. I wanna save some tape
for the Hollywood sign.

14:34.182 --> 14:38.979
- OK. Hey, thanks a lot, you guys.
- Our pleasure. Have a nice vacation, sir.

14:39.104 --> 14:40.146
Ooh!

14:42.232 --> 14:45.443
Yes... yes... yes...

14:48.571 --> 14:54.951
Cut. OK, nice take, Jenna, but let's try
giving the lines a little subtext this time.

14:55.035 --> 14:59.623
Your husband's always away on business
and you feel isolated and unloved,

14:59.748 --> 15:04.210
so you begin to think maybe
you should go back to graduate school.

15:04.335 --> 15:07.255
That's when you notice
the cable man has no pants on.

15:08.088 --> 15:12.135
Wow, a real movie set.
Hey, this house looks kinda familiar.

15:12.261 --> 15:17.264
I'll bet Samuel L Jackson is here.
He's in everything. There's Brian!

15:17.347 --> 15:23.604
All right, Samuel, when you lay her down,
I want you to enter from... Oh, my God!

15:23.729 --> 15:26.857
- Hey, you guys.
- Hey, Brian. Can I be in the movie?

15:26.940 --> 15:31.110
The Jacuzzi girl didn't show. How long
can you hold your breath under water?

15:31.235 --> 15:36.323
- Real long. One time at Hatch Pond...
- No, absolutely not. You gotta leave.

15:36.449 --> 15:40.203
- Get these people out.
- Now you're a director, we embarrass you?

15:40.286 --> 15:44.580
- No, no... I mean, yes.
- Does anyone else smell Astroglide?

15:46.667 --> 15:48.543
You're gonna look so handsome.

15:48.627 --> 15:54.464
Look at these crow's-feet. God. You stay up
past 7.30 and you pay for it in the morning.

15:54.591 --> 15:58.969
- Who the hell does Brian think he is?
- Maybe he thought we'd get in the way.

15:59.053 --> 16:02.097
It's not the first time
you've disrupted a performance.

16:07.936 --> 16:11.355
Oh, jeez. Oh, God. I didn't see it.

16:11.481 --> 16:15.318
It jumped right out in front of my car.
Oh, I am so sorry.

16:15.443 --> 16:21.990
We just have to face it. Brian's a Hollywood
director, and we're small-town people.

16:22.116 --> 16:25.660
- All right, one more. Uh, Rob Lowe?
- Straight.

16:25.744 --> 16:27.205
- No!
- Yes.

16:27.330 --> 16:28.580
- Stop.
- Ho-hum.

16:28.663 --> 16:30.749
- Pull over.
- Absolutely.

16:30.875 --> 16:33.251
- Oh, well, he hides it well.
- He wishes.

16:35.128 --> 16:38.173
Stewie. That's a funny name. Stewie.

16:38.256 --> 16:42.551
It's like stew, only with an "ie!" at the end.

16:42.634 --> 16:45.888
- Hm.
- I meant it's funny, Stewie.

16:45.972 --> 16:50.268
I had an uncle named Stewie,
and he used to sell bicycles.

16:50.268 --> 16:53.061
Aren't you supposed to be
asking me a question?

16:53.186 --> 16:57.023
What do you think candies are made out of?

16:57.148 --> 16:59.733
Sunshine and farts. What a silly question.

16:59.859 --> 17:05.073
I love candy. When I was a little boy
we would play stickball.

17:07.242 --> 17:09.535
No, no, I'll wait. Oh, you finished?

17:09.660 --> 17:14.748
Sorry. I thought the name of the show
was Kids Say the Darndest Things,

17:14.874 --> 17:18.085
not Old Black Comedians
Never Shut the Hell Up.

17:18.210 --> 17:22.588
- Ask me what I want to be when I grow up.
- And we also used to play buck-buck.

17:22.671 --> 17:27.886
Enough of your blether. Good evening, world.
From this moment on, I will be your...

17:30.721 --> 17:34.767
What you got there?
Oh, you're gonna go skiing now?

17:34.893 --> 17:37.478
Give that back. They're of no use to you.

17:37.603 --> 17:41.231
Oh, I'm going down the mountain.
Coo-coo-cachoo.

17:42.607 --> 17:44.776
No! Don't listen to him.

17:44.901 --> 17:49.780
That's not funny. That's just saying
what happens when you go skiing.

17:49.905 --> 17:51.992
Here I go, down the slope.

17:52.075 --> 17:55.829
Ooh, I'm goin' zip-zop, zooba-de-bop.

17:55.953 --> 18:00.332
Stop it. Stop applauding him.
He's not even using real words any more.

18:00.416 --> 18:06.045
We'll be back with a girl from Atlanta
who skips rope with her sister's pigtails.

18:06.170 --> 18:07.839
Coo-coo!

18:07.922 --> 18:12.927
- No, my segment's not over!
- Come on, you like to jump rope, don't ya?

18:13.886 --> 18:19.516
- I like jump rope.
- So you're gonna sit here and enjoy it.

18:19.599 --> 18:24.104
I'm gonna sit here and enjoy it.
And I like pudding.

18:24.187 --> 18:28.775
And Ghost Dad was the best movie
I've seen since Leonard Part 6.

18:32.947 --> 18:36.699
- Good news.
- What? More people I love think I'm a jerk?

18:36.824 --> 18:40.869
You're more than that, Mr "Nominated
for an Adult Movie Award for Director".

18:40.995 --> 18:45.666
- A Woody? I'm up for a Woody?
- Call your family. They'll be proud of you.

18:45.791 --> 18:48.711
I'd rather they think I'm a jerk
than a smut pedlar.

18:48.794 --> 18:52.672
They'll love you even if you made
a couple of crappy movies.

18:52.756 --> 18:56.925
